      "supplements": {},
      "note": "Fresh GPT-6.1 Sol complete visual reading of all 22 source pages (7 question, 15 key), including matching supervisor/cover and STOP pages in both documents. Six whole original problems with native numbers A1–A4 and B1–B2; A1 5 native parts, A4 4, B1 8 roman tasks grouped under their three lettered stems, B2 4 task leaves with the printed c stem attached to c.i, A2/A3 unpartitioned. Common instructions/constants transcribed once from main question pages 1–2 and STOP note page 5. Official key repeated questions and B2 graphic shown once, all complete solution reasoning and alternatives retained. A1 second V_0 and “fat”, A2 graph description reversal, A4 frequency relation, and B2 “in terms any or all” retained exactly as printed. Reused historical draft as transcription scaffold after full source reading; every source paragraph, formula and table checked against actual pages. Historical files and provenance unchanged; current reader/provenance is this GPT-6.1 Sol reading. All proposed crops use personally chosen boxes with no snapping; final actual crops and MDX inspected before handoff. No separate model checker. Native alphanumeric question numbers are stored exactly as printed; the validator reports its generic non-integer-number warnings for A1–B2. The STOP divider belongs only to the boundary following A4; its full text is attached to A4 after the task, rather than repeated after every unrelated problem."
    }
